 that i thought it was  ventriloquism because how is he going to  ask himself questions but obviously he's  got a co-counsel who is there i would  imagine that he has pre-written  questions and they would go over  everything that he would like to have  come out but as far as the objections  because he is a he's he's representing  himself and if he's under direct is he  going to be able to object to some of  the questions based on that i don't know  but i'd like to see him take the stand  i think a lot of people would with him  representing himself it certainly is  making for an interesting trial  when we come back a heated start to the  day in an ohio courtroom  ahead of both sides resting in the case  of matthew moore as he stands trial for  the stage  suicide of his wife  [Music]  welcome back in ohio things got a little  heated in the courtroom before the  defense began presenting their case for  the day in the trial of matthew moore as  he faces murder charges for the alleged  staged suicide death of his estranged  wife the trial comes more than two years  after emily noble was last seen the  night of her 52nd birthday celebration  when she and moore went out on may 24  2020. moore reported noble missing but  he reportedly never helped with the  search for his wife over the next few  months then four months later several  women found noble's body badly  decomposed in the woods near the  couple's home her remains were in a  kneeling position with a usb cord around  her neck tied to a tree branch  authorities believe she was murdered and  that her death was staged to look like a  suicide moore was arrested last june and  charged with felony murder and assault  in connection to noble's death before  the jury was brought in on thursday  morning attorneys had a dispute with the  judge then one of the prosecutors  stormed out take a look  yeah i'm sorry but i would object to  going forward anyway right now without  the elected county prosecutor who's on  this case but she chose not to be here  that's not accurate judge okay  okay your objections noted we had a  phone status conference two weeks ago in  which  bishop your objection is noted  okay  i'm not going to participate in this  proceeding without the elected county  prosecutor i think this is a shame that  you're going forward when the court was  you're going to sit here  you're going to sit here you were told  about her unavailability and  specifically told her on the phone not  to cancel that appointment that it  wouldn't be i'll tell you what if you  want to be here for the decision that's  your business well your honor i think  this is outrageous you're going for  without the prosecutors  once testimony did get underway the  defense rested after their second  witness he testified about a test he  conducted with a crash dummy on the  branch where noble's remains were found  after the  static mass test did you do a second  test on the branch  we did and and we called that the  dynamic test and we started by just  hanging that fifth female small female  crash test dummy  to make sure the branch just found the  dummy and then we tried to  uh lift the dummy about six inches  and and give it a little bit of a  dynamic event  so that there was some energy from  gravity pulling on the dummy back down  i really wanted to try to mimic exactly  how the remains were discovered to make  sure the test was realistic as possible  was the branch able to sustain those  five tests  the branch did not fail so i would say  sustain the five tests  and lisa let's start with you here have  you ever seen a prosecutor storm out of  a courtroom and legally could the case  even continue without anyone from the  prosecution team present  no this was the first time that i've  seen something like that um complete  lack of decorum i totally understand  what he was trying to say to the judge  he didn't want to continue the judge was  aware of her not being present for that  period of time and the only way that it  would continue obviously he cooled his  heels and he came back is to have  somebody else pinch hit for  the state's attorney who was not able to  be there or the judge could simply say  let's have an adjournment and give him a  day to resolve the issue  certainly made for a dramatic moment in  that courtroom terry turning now to the  defense council in this case how is she  doing and was this a good witness to  call  well i think she's doing a great job and  it was a very necessary witness diane  monash the defense counsel she's tried  over 100 cases in fact she tried that  case against dr william husell who was  the individual who was accused frankly  of murdering his patients and she got 14  not guilty verdicts for him she teaches  at harvard law school so she is not a  novice her opening statement detailed  what she was going to show and i liked  that she didn't just sit back and let  the prosecution fail she said to that  jury i am going to show you what this  case is all about and this particular  witness was important that witness could  establish that that tree could hold a  body and from a forensic standpoint that  is extremely important the jury has to  understand that this possibility this  suicide could have existed and so that  witness was crucial and really all the  defense needs to do is to make sure just  one of those jurors has some sort of  reasonable doubt and by putting this  witness on she has established that  she's also said she's bringing other  witnesses and if she does that i do  think that the jury will be able to  think about the fact that this case has  doubt and maybe that will be an  acquittal or you know maybe a hung jury  yeah and certainly not a lot of evidence  in this case thank you both lisa and  terry and to our viewers thank you for  joining us here on law and crime daily  we'll see you next time  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

